**Configuring Sendmail with Amazon SES SMTP Relay for Monitoring Email Alerts**

## Overview

A request was received to configure the mail service on multiple Linux servers to enable email notifications from monitoring scripts.

The solution used **Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)** as the outbound SMTP relay. After the AWS team completed the SES setup and verified 
the domain identity, Sendmail was configured on each server to relay emails through the Amazon SES SMTP endpoint.

Following the configuration, test emails were sent successfully from all servers, confirming that monitoring scripts could deliver email alerts.

